{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"Updated only the two returned Drafted rows; statuses remain unchanged.\n\n- LLR-362 `detail`\n  - Before: `\"The carrier holds the id watermark for every lane-minted space. A reservation moves the carrier by compare-and-swap ... Every watermark writer preserves the records it receives.\"`\n  - After: `\"The carrier is a shared ref holding the id watermark for every lane-minted space apart from any lane's branch. A reservation moves the carrier by compare-and-swap ... A mark rises only by allocation, a ruled correction, or a covering reservation record.\"`\n  - Why: closes all five return gaps: carrier identity, high-water range floor/disjointness, zero-write refusals, first-use seeding, fold output/basis, and mark-rise authority.\n\n- TC-401 `expected`\n  - Before: `\"Each admitted reservation receives a range above its applicable high-water mark; each refused reservation leaves both durable states unchanged; concurrent and sequential reservations are disjoint; a lost swap leaves no reservation; and each fold preserves the highest marks and every valid record exactly once.\"`\n  - After: `\"Each admitted reservation receives a range one above its applicable carrier or integration-branch high-water mark; each refused reservation leaves both durable states unchanged; concurrent and sequential reservations are disjoint; a lost swap leaves no reservation; the first reservation creates a carrier seeded from the integration branch's committed watermark; and each fold preserves the highest marks and every valid record exactly once.\"`\n  - Why: adds the missing first-use arm and makes the claimed allocation floor explicit.\n\nSitting-return points:\n\n- Carrier is a shared ref outside lane branches: done; `CARRIER_REF`, `carrier_tip`, and `carrier_text` hold it.\n- Range starts above the larger carrier/trunk committed mark: done; `plan_reservation` computes `max(carrier, trunk) + 1`.\n- Sequential/concurrent reservations are disjoint: done; carrier ref update is compare-and-swap, with `test_sequential_reservations_are_disjoint` and `test_stale_base_reservations_are_disjoint`.\n- Refused argument or lost compare-and-swap writes nothing: done; `reserve` validates before writing, and `write_carrier` refuses a failed ref update. Evidence includes `test_each_reserve_refusal_writes_nothing` and `test_a_lost_race_refuses_with_nothing_written`.\n- First use seeds from integration branch committed watermark: done; `reserve` supplies the trunk watermark when no carrier exists. Evidence: `test_first_reservation_seeds_the_carrier_from_trunk`.\n- Fold maximums, record union, and receiving-tree live-id basis: done; `fold` produces the maximum/union and `fold_watermark` renders with `_basis(live_max_ids(root))`. Evidence includes `test_the_fold_takes_each_spaces_maximum_and_the_union_of_records`, `test_the_fold_collapses_duplicates_and_sorts_by_space_then_low`, and `test_fold_ids_on_a_conflicted_watermark`.\n- Mark-rise rule: done; `_mark_history_findings` permits allocation/live coverage, reservation coverage, or an exact ruled correction; TC-158 remains its direct verifier.\n- TC-401 first-use expectation: done; added as above, with existing evidence already naming the test.\n\nAll TC-401 evidence functions were found; no missing test to report.\n\nPer instruction, I did not run strict lints or pytest."}}
